Scrutiny of private credit in Australia
Increased regulatory attention in Australia over conduct in the private credit market. 

ASIC (Australian Securities & Investments Commission) has flagged poor risk and valuation disclosures, conflicts of interest, inconsistent terminology. 

Some funds have been frozen or restricted due to transparency issues and investor protections. 

The sector is responding via pledges to develop stronger industry standards to avoid tighter regulation. 



Private markets mis‐selling and illiquidity risk in Europe / UK
As private market products become more accessible to wealthy individuals in Europe, warnings are growing about mis‐selling (especially around illiquidity). 

Semi-liquid funds in UK/Europe have ballooned (e.g. ~€88 billion), making risk understanding more critical. 
